.TH elfshaker-clone 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-clone \- Create a working directory configured from a remote index.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker clone\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> <\fIDIRECTORY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new working directory, configures the supplied .esi index as the `origin` remote, and downloads its pack indexes. Pack payloads are fetched on demand. The destination must not exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>
URL of the remote .esi index.
.TP
<\fIDIRECTORY\fR>
New working directory to create.
.SH EXAMPLES
Clone the public manyclangs remote, which provides snapshots of prebuilt LLVM versions:
.PP
.nf
\fBelfshaker clone \\\fR
.br
\fB  https://github.com/elfshaker/manyclangs/releases/download/v0.9.0/aarch64\-ubuntu2004.esi \\\fR
.br
\fB  manyclangs\fR
.fi
.PP
This creates a working directory named manyclangs and downloads its pack indexes. Pack data is fetched when a snapshot is needed.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
manyclangs project:
.UR https://github.com/elfshaker/manyclangs
https://github.com/elfshaker/manyclangs
.UE
